## Implementation Steps

1. Create `empire-pipeline-runner.py`:
   - CLI: `python empire-pipeline-runner.py --mode empire` (default) or `--mode v16` (legacy)
   - Empire mode flow:
     a. Run pain-signal-miner + platform-shift-detector (parallel via subprocess)
     b. Run founder-edge-matcher on combined signals
     c. Run compound-filter on matched signals
     d. For PASS signals: invoke V16 deep-reasoner (existing agent)
     e. Run staircase-enforcer on results
     f. Output: `{empire_verdicts: [{name, verdict, compound_score, timing_score, stair_allowed, reasons}]}`
   - Save results to `data/empire/pipeline-runs/run-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM.json`

2. Update transaction-layer SKILL.md:
   - Add "Empire Mode" section documenting new pipeline
   - Keep V16 mode as default, empire mode as opt-in
   - Document: `--mode empire` flag for empire pipeline

3. Create verdict taxonomy:
   - `GO_EMPIRE` — compound score ≥3, timing ≥6, staircase allowed, deep-reasoner positive
   - `GO_BRIDGE` — compound score 2 (DOWNGRADE), staircase allows (Stair 0-1), good for cash bridge
   - `KILL` — compound score ≤1, or staircase blocks, or deep-reasoner negative

4. Wire ground truth capture:
   - After verdict: prompt to record decision via ground-truth-cli.py
   - After 30 days: prompt to record outcome
   - Feed outcome into compound-dashboard for learning

5. Test end-to-end: run empire pipeline with 3 mock opportunities (SaaS, freelance, template)

## Success Criteria
- [ ] empire-pipeline-runner.py runs full pipeline end-to-end
- [ ] V16 legacy mode still works unchanged
- [ ] Verdicts correctly classified (GO_EMPIRE, GO_BRIDGE, KILL)
- [ ] Results saved to pipeline-runs directory
- [ ] Ground truth capture wired at end of pipeline
- [ ] 3 mock opportunities produce correct verdicts

## Risk Assessment
- Risk: Pipeline too slow (many scripts) → Mitigation: parallel execution for signal collectors
- Risk: Breaking V16 → Mitigation: empire mode is separate flag, V16 default unchanged
